---
description: Rules for the theratax project
alwaysApply: true
---

# Stack
- NestJS 12 as an ES module ("type": "module") + TypeScript strict on Node.js 24
- PostgreSQL via Prisma 7 only, accessed through the injected PrismaService — never `new PrismaClient` in another file
- Validation with class-validator + class-transformer via DTO classes (never use an interface as a body). Global ValidationPipe uses whitelist and forbidNonWhitelisted

# File structure
- src/<domain>/ one folder per business domain (auth, transactions, tax-engine, expense-categories, upload, invoices), containing *.module.ts, *.controller.ts, *.service.ts and dto/. /users/me lives in auth
- src/prisma/ contains PrismaModule (global) and PrismaService
- src/generated/prisma/ is Prisma-generated code — never edit it by hand
- docs/api-spec.md is the API contract — every endpoint's response must match this file's shape. Phase 2 listed there is out of scope

# Coding rules
- Imports of project files must always end in .js (e.g. './transactions.service.js'), even though the actual file is .ts
- Use `import type` for interfaces/types that appear in the signature of a method or constructor that has a decorator
- Never use `any`, never use `as` to silence a type error, never use the non-null assertion (!), and every decorated parameter must declare a type
- Errors returned to the client must be thrown as Nest's HttpException (NotFoundException, BadRequestException, UnauthorizedException, ForbiddenException, ConflictException) — never throw a plain Error
- Name files kebab-case.<role>.ts, e.g. transactions.controller.ts, create-transaction.dto.ts
- Responses must be plain JSON (number, string, array, object) — never send a Date or a Decimal. Money is integer pence. Civil dates are YYYY-MM-DD. Timestamps are ISO 8601
- The tax engine is a pure function with unit tests. HTTP handlers load data and call it; they do not contain the arithmetic

# Scope
- Never install a new dependency unless asked
- Keep changes limited to what the request's goal needs — never touch unrelated files
- Never create index.ts or a barrel file
- Never write a comment that just explains what the code already says
- Never run prisma migrate, db push, generate, or docker yourself — tell the user to run it
